          "code": "import numpy as np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(301)\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# First-Principles NumPy: Reliability Table, Uniform vs Quantile ECE/MCE,\n# dan Bukti Invariansi ROC-AUC di Bawah Distorsi Overconfidence Monoton\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nn = 4000\nz_true = rng.normal(loc=-1.1, scale=1.45, size=n)\np_true = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-z_true))\ny = rng.binomial(1, p_true)\n\n# Model A: Probabilitas terkalibrasi baik (sedikit noise estimasi)\np_cal = np.clip(1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(z_true + rng.normal(0, 0.08, n)))), 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n# Model B: Transformasi monoton overconfident (logit dikali 2.8x — mirip NN modern!)\np_over = np.clip(1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(2.8 * z_true))), 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n# Model C: Transformasi monoton underconfident (logit diredam 0.35x — mirip RF/SVM!)\np_under = np.clip(1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(0.35 * z_true))), 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n\ndef roc_auc_manual(y_true: np.ndarray, scores: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    order = np.argsort(-scores, kind=\"mergesort\")\n    ys = y_true[order]\n    tp = np.cumsum(ys)\n    fp = np.cumsum(1 - ys)\n    tpr = np.r_[0.0, tp / tp[-1]]\n    fpr = np.r_[0.0, fp / fp[-1]]\n    return float(np.trapezoid(tpr, fpr))\n\n\ndef ece_mce_from_scratch(\n    y_true: np.ndarray, probs: np.ndarray, n_bins: int = 10, strategy: str = \"uniform\"\n) -> tuple[float, float, list[tuple[int, float, float]]]:\n    if strategy == \"uniform\":\n        edges = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n    else:\n        edges = np.quantile(probs, np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1))\n        edges[0], edges[-1] = 0.0, 1.0\n\n    ece, mce = 0.0, 0.0\n    bins_info: list[tuple[int, float, float]] = []\n    total = len(y_true)\n    for b in range(n_bins):\n        lo, hi = edges[b], edges[b + 1]\n        if b == n_bins - 1:\n            mask = (probs >= lo) & (probs <= hi)\n        else:\n            mask = (probs >= lo) & (probs < hi)\n        cnt = int(np.sum(mask))\n        if cnt == 0:\n            continue\n        acc_b = float(np.mean(y_true[mask]))\n        conf_b = float(np.mean(probs[mask]))\n        gap = abs(acc_b - conf_b)\n        ece += (cnt / total) * gap\n        mce = max(mce, gap)\n        bins_info.append((cnt, conf_b, acc_b))\n    return ece, mce, bins_info\n\n\nprint(f\"=== Audit Kalibrasi First-Principles (N={n}, Prevalensi={y.mean():.3f}) ===\")\nfor label, p in [\n    (\"Model A (Terkalibrasi)\", p_cal),\n    (\"Model B (Overconfident 2.8x)\", p_over),\n    (\"Model C (Underconfident 0.35x)\", p_under),\n]:\n    auc_v = roc_auc_manual(y, p)\n    brier = float(np.mean((p - y) ** 2))\n    nll = float(-np.mean(y * np.log(p) + (1 - y) * np.log(1 - p)))\n    ece_u, mce_u, _ = ece_mce_from_scratch(y, p, n_bins=10, strategy=\"uniform\")\n    ece_q, mce_q, _ = ece_mce_from_scratch(y, p, n_bins=10, strategy=\"quantile\")\n    print(\n        f\"{label:31s} | AUC={auc_v:.4f} | Brier={brier:.4f} | NLL={nll:.4f} | \"\n        f\"ECE(U)={ece_u:.4f} | ECE(Q)={ece_q:.4f} | MCE(Q)={mce_q:.4f}\"\n    )\n\nprint(\"\\nReliability Table 5-Bin Kuantil (Model B Overconfident):\")\n_, _, info_b = ece_mce_from_scratch(y, p_over, n_bins=5, strategy=\"quantile\")\nfor idx, (cnt, conf_b, acc_b) in enumerate(info_b, 1):\n    print(f\"  Bin Q{idx} (n={cnt:3d}) | Mean Pred={conf_b:.4f} | Actual Freq={acc_b:.4f} | Gap={conf_b - acc_b:+.4f}\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== Audit Kalibrasi First-Principles (N=4000, Prevalensi=0.304) ===\nModel A (Terkalibrasi)          | AUC=0.8108 | Brier=0.1561 | NLL=0.4750 | ECE(U)=0.0173 | ECE(Q)=0.0130 | MCE(Q)=0.0266\nModel B (Overconfident 2.8x)    | AUC=0.8112 | Brier=0.1778 | NLL=0.6573 | ECE(U)=0.1328 | ECE(Q)=0.1300 | MCE(Q)=0.2129\nModel C (Underconfident 0.35x)  | AUC=0.8112 | Brier=0.1833 | NLL=0.5524 | ECE(U)=0.1479 | ECE(Q)=0.1484 | MCE(Q)=0.2344\n\nReliability Table 5-Bin Kuantil (Model B Overconfident):\n  Bin Q1 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.0005 | Actual Freq=0.0437 | Gap=-0.0433\n  Bin Q2 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.0071 | Actual Freq=0.1250 | Gap=-0.1179\n  Bin Q3 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.0517 | Actual Freq=0.2512 | Gap=-0.1996\n  Bin Q4 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.3083 | Actual Freq=0.4175 | Gap=-0.1092\n  Bin Q5 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.8625 | Actual Freq=0.6825 | Gap=+0.1800",
          "actualOutput": "=== Audit Kalibrasi First-Principles (N=4000, Prevalensi=0.304) ===\nModel A (Terkalibrasi)          | AUC=0.8108 | Brier=0.1561 | NLL=0.4750 | ECE(U)=0.0173 | ECE(Q)=0.0130 | MCE(Q)=0.0266\nModel B (Overconfident 2.8x)    | AUC=0.8112 | Brier=0.1778 | NLL=0.6573 | ECE(U)=0.1328 | ECE(Q)=0.1300 | MCE(Q)=0.2129\nModel C (Underconfident 0.35x)  | AUC=0.8112 | Brier=0.1833 | NLL=0.5524 | ECE(U)=0.1479 | ECE(Q)=0.1484 | MCE(Q)=0.2344\n\nReliability Table 5-Bin Kuantil (Model B Overconfident):\n  Bin Q1 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.0005 | Actual Freq=0.0437 | Gap=-0.0433\n  Bin Q2 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.0071 | Actual Freq=0.1250 | Gap=-0.1179\n  Bin Q3 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.0517 | Actual Freq=0.2512 | Gap=-0.1996\n  Bin Q4 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.3083 | Actual Freq=0.4175 | Gap=-0.1092\n  Bin Q5 (n=800) | Mean Pred=0.8625 | Actual Freq=0.6825 | Gap=+0.1800",
