          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize_scalar\n\ndef temperature_scale_logits(logits_cal, y_cal, logits_test, y_test) -> tuple[float, float, float, bool]:\n    lc = np.asarray(logits_cal, dtype=float)\n    yc = np.asarray(y_cal, dtype=int)\n    lt = np.asarray(logits_test, dtype=float)\n    yt = np.asarray(y_test, dtype=int)\n    def nll_at(logits, y, T):\n        z = logits / T\n        z = z - np.max(z, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        log_p = z - np.log(np.sum(np.exp(z), axis=1, keepdims=True))\n        return float(-np.mean(log_p[np.arange(len(y)), y]))\n    opt = minimize_scalar(lambda T: nll_at(lc, yc, T), bounds=(0.1, 10.0), method='bounded')\n    T_opt = float(opt.x)\n    nll_before = nll_at(lt, yt, 1.0)\n    nll_after = nll_at(lt, yt, T_opt)\n    same_argmax = bool(np.array_equal(np.argmax(lt, axis=1), np.argmax(lt / T_opt, axis=1)))\n    return (round(T_opt, 4), round(nll_before, 4), round(nll_after, 4), same_argmax)\n```"
