          "code": "import numpy as np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(304)\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# First-Principles NumPy: Heteroscedastic Data — Mengapa Split Conformal Standar\n# & Gaussian Naif Gagal Conditional Coverage di Ekor Varians Tinggi vs CQR!\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nn_cal, n_test = 1000, 2000\nalpha = 0.10\n\n\ndef gen_heteroscedastic(n: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    x = rng.uniform(0.0, 10.0, size=n)\n    mu = 3.0 + 1.5 * np.sin(x) + 0.4 * x\n    # Simpangan baku tumbuh 6x lipat dari x=0 (sigma=0.4) ke x=10 (sigma=2.8)!\n    sigma = 0.4 + 0.24 * x\n    y = mu + sigma * rng.standard_normal(size=n)\n    return x, y, mu\n\n\nx_cal, y_cal, mu_cal = gen_heteroscedastic(n_cal)\nx_te, y_te, mu_te = gen_heteroscedastic(n_test)\n\n# Estimasi kuantil awal yang sedikit under-covered (sengaja 0.72x skala sejati, mirip ML overfit!)\nq_lo_cal = mu_cal - 1.18 * (0.4 + 0.24 * x_cal)\nq_hi_cal = mu_cal + 1.18 * (0.4 + 0.24 * x_cal)\nq_lo_te = mu_te - 1.18 * (0.4 + 0.24 * x_te)\nq_hi_te = mu_te + 1.18 * (0.4 + 0.24 * x_te)\n\nq_lvl = np.ceil((n_cal + 1) * (1.0 - alpha)) / n_cal\n\n# 1) Gaussian Naif Homoscedastic: mu +/- 1.6449 * sigma_global\nsig_glob = float(np.std(y_cal - mu_cal, ddof=1))\nlo_g, hi_g = mu_te - 1.6449 * sig_glob, mu_te + 1.6449 * sig_glob\n\n# 2) Split Conformal Standar (lebar konstan 2*q_sc)\nq_sc = float(np.quantile(np.abs(y_cal - mu_cal), q_lvl, method=\"higher\"))\nlo_sc, hi_sc = mu_te - q_sc, mu_te + q_sc\n\n# 3) Raw Quantile Regression (tanpa conformalization -> under-covered!)\nlo_qr, hi_qr = q_lo_te, q_hi_te\n\n# 4) CQR (Romano et al. 2019): skor bertanda E_i = max(q_lo - y, y - q_hi)\nE_cal = np.maximum(q_lo_cal - y_cal, y_cal - q_hi_cal)\nq_cqr = float(np.quantile(E_cal, q_lvl, method=\"higher\"))\nlo_cqr, hi_cqr = q_lo_te - q_cqr, q_hi_te + q_cqr\n\nlow_var = x_te < 3.33\nmid_var = (x_te >= 3.33) & (x_te < 6.67)\nhigh_var = x_te >= 6.67\n\nprint(f\"=== Audit Conditional Coverage Data Heteroskedastik (Target=90%, CQR Q_hat={q_cqr:+.3f}) ===\")\nfor name, lo, hi in [\n    (\"1. Gaussian Naif (+/-1.645s)\", lo_g, hi_g),\n    (\"2. Split Conformal (Konstan)\", lo_sc, hi_sc),\n    (\"3. Raw Quantile (Uncalibrated)\", lo_qr, hi_qr),\n    (\"4. CQR Adaptif (Romano 2019)\", lo_cqr, hi_cqr),\n]:\n    hit = (y_te >= lo) & (y_te <= hi)\n    w = hi - lo\n    print(\n        f\"{name:30s} | Marg={hit.mean():.3f} | LowVar={hit[low_var].mean():.3f} | \"\n        f\"MidVar={hit[mid_var].mean():.3f} | HighVar={hit[high_var].mean():.3f} | AvgW={w.mean():.2f}\"\n    )",
          "expectedOutput": "=== Audit Conditional Coverage Data Heteroskedastik (Target=90%, CQR Q_hat=+0.678) ===\n1. Gaussian Naif (+/-1.645s)   | Marg=0.903 | LowVar=0.999 | MidVar=0.924 | HighVar=0.772 | AvgW=5.60\n2. Split Conformal (Konstan)   | Marg=0.912 | LowVar=1.000 | MidVar=0.935 | HighVar=0.788 | AvgW=5.85\n3. Raw Quantile (Uncalibrated) | Marg=0.760 | LowVar=0.756 | MidVar=0.748 | HighVar=0.778 | AvgW=3.70\n4. CQR Adaptif (Romano 2019)   | Marg=0.906 | LowVar=0.959 | MidVar=0.891 | HighVar=0.861 | AvgW=5.05",
          "actualOutput": "=== Audit Conditional Coverage Data Heteroskedastik (Target=90%, CQR Q_hat=+0.678) ===\n1. Gaussian Naif (+/-1.645s)   | Marg=0.903 | LowVar=0.999 | MidVar=0.924 | HighVar=0.772 | AvgW=5.60\n2. Split Conformal (Konstan)   | Marg=0.912 | LowVar=1.000 | MidVar=0.935 | HighVar=0.788 | AvgW=5.85\n3. Raw Quantile (Uncalibrated) | Marg=0.760 | LowVar=0.756 | MidVar=0.748 | HighVar=0.778 | AvgW=3.70\n4. CQR Adaptif (Romano 2019)   | Marg=0.906 | LowVar=0.959 | MidVar=0.891 | HighVar=0.861 | AvgW=5.05",
