          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cqr_calibrate_and_evaluate(q_lo_cal, q_hi_cal, y_cal, q_lo_test, q_hi_test, y_test, alpha: float = 0.20) -> tuple[float, float, float, float]:\n    qlc, qhc, yc = np.asarray(q_lo_cal, dtype=float), np.asarray(q_hi_cal, dtype=float), np.asarray(y_cal, dtype=float)\n    qlt, qht, yt = np.asarray(q_lo_test, dtype=float), np.asarray(q_hi_test, dtype=float), np.asarray(y_test, dtype=float)\n    scores = np.maximum(qlc - yc, yc - qhc)\n    n = len(scores)\n    q_level = min(1.0, float(np.ceil((n + 1) * (1.0 - alpha)) / n))\n    q_hat = float(np.quantile(scores, q_level, method='higher'))\n    raw_cov = float(np.mean((yt >= qlt) & (yt <= qht)))\n    lo_cqr, hi_cqr = qlt - q_hat, qht + q_hat\n    cqr_cov = float(np.mean((yt >= lo_cqr) & (yt <= hi_cqr)))\n    avg_w = float(np.mean(hi_cqr - lo_cqr))\n    return (round(q_hat, 4), round(raw_cov, 4), round(cqr_cov, 4), round(avg_w, 4))\n```"
